# Data files are written by Python's text-mode open(), which emits CRLF on
# Windows, while the hosted Linux runner writes LF. Letting git normalize them
# made data/liveness.json and the jsonl ledgers permanently "modified" in the
# working tree, which blocked every merge with the runner and cost a stash
# round-trip that nearly stranded 4 rows of real data.
#
# These are append-only records, not source. Git should store the bytes it is
# given and stop rewriting them.
data/** -text
*.jsonl -text
